/target
node_modules/
apps/desktop/build/
apps/desktop/.svelte-kit/
apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen/
.DS_Store

# AI-agent session scratch — never part of the repo
.superpowers/
.remember/
.claude/settings.local.json
# Skills installed per-machine by whoever is working here. Not project-owned:
# they carry their own compiled artefacts (__pycache__), they differ per person,
# and committing one would ship someone's local tooling to everyone who clones.
#
# `**/` and not a bare `.claude/skills/`: a pattern with an interior slash is
# ANCHORED to the directory holding this file, so the bare form covered the repo
# root and nothing else. A skill dropped in apps/desktop/ or crates/ would have
# been committed. Verified with `git check-ignore` before and after this change,
# not assumed from the docs.
**/.claude/skills/
# The isolated worktrees this repo's agent workflow creates live under here too.
**/.claude/worktrees/

# The package build pipeline (build/). The driver, the audit and the recipes are
# the repo's; nothing they produce is. A MariaDB build tree is 3.4 GB and the
# installed tree 465 MB, so one careless `git add` is a repository nobody can
# clone. The default output directory is excluded outright, and the artifact
# shapes are excluded wherever under build/ they land, because an artifact that
# is merely in an unusual place is still an artifact.
#
# `/build/` and not `build/`: a leading slash anchors this to the repo root, so
# it cannot swallow a `build/` directory inside a crate or an app. Verified with
# `git check-ignore -v`, not assumed.
/build/out/
/build/**/*.tar.gz
/build/**/*.tar.xz
/build/**/*.tgz
/build/**/*.sha256
/build/**/*.manifest.json
